        <body>
            <div xml:id="d254">

                <pb facs="0774" n="739" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76v39/pg739"/>

                <head>254. Memorandum From the Counselor of the Department of State (Sonnenfeldt) to
                    Secretary of State Kissinger<anchor n="1" xml:id="d254-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1974-10-04">October 4, 1974</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Mr. Secretary,</p>
                <p>I have prepared an up-date for your luncheon with Dobrynin on the
                        following:<anchor n="2" xml:id="d254-f2"/>
                    <list>
                        <item>Tab A—The Trade Bill</item>
                        <item>Tab B—Moscow talks on nuclear issues</item>
                        <item>Tab C—CSCE </item>
                        <item>Tab D—MBFR </item>
                        <item>Tab E—Chemical Weapons</item>
                        <pb facs="0775" n="740" xml:id="pg740"/>
                        <item>Tab F—Environmental Warfare</item>
                        <item>Tab G—The Grain Deal</item>
                        <item>Tab H—UN Financing</item>
                        <item>Tab I—The EXIM Bank Bill</item>
                    </list>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#bold">HS</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d254-a1.xml" xpointer="d254-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d254-a2.xml" xpointer="d254-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d254-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d254-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, RG 59, Records of the Office of the Counselor, Entry
                    5339, Box 8, Soviet Union, October 1974. Secret; Eyes Only. Kissinger wrote at
                    the bottom of the first page, “List of participants.”</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d254-f2" n="2" xml:id="d254-f2-content">
                <p>Tabs A–B and E–I are attached but not printed. No record of Kissinger’s luncheon
                    meeting with Dobrynin has been found.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
